Against an opener policy, Ladybird now checks only the sandboxing flags
a navigation brings, not the spec’s finalSandboxFlags, which also take
in the response’s own CSP sandbox. Blink, WebKit and Gecko all do the
same: Blink’s CrossOriginOpenerPolicyStatus::SanitizeResponse() checks
frame_tree_node_->pending_frame_policy().sandbox_flags, WebKit’s
doCrossOriginOpenerHandlingOfResponse() checks the frame’s own
effectiveSandboxFlags(), and Gecko’s HttpBaseChannel::
ComputeCrossOriginOpenerPolicyMismatch() checks mLoadInfo->
GetSandboxFlags(). The WPT test coop-navigate-same-origin-csp-sandbox.
html expects a page that sandboxes itself that way to load.
